Computers are good with numbers.
&ldquo;what&rsquo;s bigger, centillition to the power of a centillion, or a googolplex?&rdquo;
I am glad that Google gives me a richly sourced and well reasoned answer, linked below:
&ldquo;A googolplex is vastly bigger than a centillion to the power of a centillion.&rdquo;
The Math
Centillion: In the short scale, a centillion is 10^303 (a 1 followed by 303 zeros) Centillion to the power of a centillion: (10^303)^(10^303) which is roughly 10^(10^305.48). Googol and Googolplex: A googol is 10^100 A googolplex is 10^googol = 10^(10^100). Why a Googolplex Wins
Centillion to the centillion power is roughly 10^(a number with about 305 digits). A googolplex is 10^(a number with 101 digits), which is orders of magnitude larger. To put it in perspective, a googolplex is so large that writing out all of its zeros in decimal form would require more paper and matter than exists in the known physical universe.&quot;
Please don&rsquo;t outsource your thinking skills yet.
Link to answer

